# JayLexi mid-field surf-row strength (thread "Take 1st with JayLexi and Sanaro"; BENCH-179). JayLexi 0.4 is 4th in
# MiniRumble on 88.21, 0.25 behind 3rd (Foilist). Live (docs/bench/live-kitlab-0.3.md, "0.4 live"), the gap to FoilistMC
# outside the top 30 is ranks 61-450, about -0.5 together, small per bot but many bots. This card asks how hard JayLexi
# should lean on each mid-field opponent's own surf row.
#   ./queue.sh run pc-jaylexi-mid        (or  .\queue.ps1 run pc-jaylexi-mid)
# Run it from master with this card merged: git checkout master && git pull
# One bench queue, RoboRumble workers at 0, unpinned. Nothing here touches Hadur or the shipped JayLexi; nothing is
# uploaded or released.
#
# Why it should win (the PC card rule of 2026-11-03):
# - Per-opponent tailoring only: each arm changes the AIM rows (where that named robot aimed at us) of ranks 121-450, and
#   nothing else, at the same 1,494 B. The top 120 keep 0.4's field row, the rest keep 0.4's rows.
# - Those rows are the one lever that has shown live on this field: 0.3's rows gained +1.4 to +1.7 a bot on ranks 121-450
#   over 0.2, and 0.4 kept them. Their weight (peak 2000) was never tuned: it was set once, beside a field row of 100.
#   These robots mostly carry simple, repeatable guns, so their harvested aim should predict well, and leaning harder
#   (p4, peak 4000) should dodge more of it. If the rows are over-trusted against the ones that adapt, p1 (peak 1000) wins.
# - Risk: the optimum may sit at 2000 already, and then both arms lose; the pilot ends that early.
#
# Pilot: shuffled jobs, so the first 20% (640 battles) are a fair sample. At 20% the futility rule finishes the run if
# neither p1 nor p4 can still reach a gain above 0 (z 3), and the A/A rule halts it if aa is out of its band against c.
# Otherwise it runs on to 3,200 battles.
#
# Ranks here count the other robots only (our own two left out of the 2026-11-02 list), so 121-450 is global 123-452;
# the arms and the panel use the same numbering, so every panel robot is one whose row the arms change.
# Panel: kitlab/mini-mid-field.txt, 80 robots, one from each even rank band of MiniRumble ranks 121-450 (seed 8), none in
# broken-1.11.2.txt, on Robocode 1.11.2. 4 arms x 80 robots x 10 fresh seeds from 9700 x 35 rounds.
# Read: each arm against c and aa pooled, per opponent, mean and 95% over the 80; per band (1: 121-250, 2: 251-450). The
# panel stands for 330 of 669 pairings, so the whole-field APS gain is the panel gain x 0.49. An arm passes when its 95%
# low end is above 0; a pass ships as JayLexi 0.5 on Leigh's word only.
# Stop rules: fails 30, dead 8, skips 60 over 200, stall 30m (halt; every battle fought is kept and a rerun resumes),
# aa after 20% (halt), futility p1,p4 below 0 after 20% (finish: the gate and results PR run on the battles so far).
# ALERT opens an issue for Leigh on a stop.

set C = --skip-build --skip-fetch --rounds 35 --parallel auto --child-heap 512M --no-truth-log
set SRC = ../jaylexi/src/main/java/hadur117/mini/JayLexi.java
set RANK = ../data/rumble/parsed/2026-11-02T1440Z_minirumble_rankings.json
set W = work/jaylexi-mid
set OUT = ../docs/bench/local
set ALERT = lgriffin
set REL = https://github.com/lgriffin/Hadur_Robot/releases/download

prep | git checkout -q master && mkdir -p ${W} kitlab/jars && ./fetch-opponents.sh --set kitlab/mini-mid-field.txt && mvn -q compile && curl -fsSL -o kitlab/jars/hadur117.mini.JayLexi_0.4.jar ${REL}/jaylexi-v0.4/hadur117.mini.JayLexi_0.4.jar && python3 tools/jaylexi_rows_off.py ${SRC} ${W}/p1000.java --rankings ${RANK} --top 450 --skip 120 --peak 1000 && python3 tools/jaylexi_rows_off.py ${SRC} ${W}/p4000.java --rankings ${RANK} --top 450 --skip 120 --peak 4000 && bash kitlab/build_arm.sh ${SRC} hadur117.mini.JayLexi 0.4aa && bash kitlab/build_arm.sh ${W}/p1000.java hadur117.mini.JayLexi 0.4p1000 && bash kitlab/build_arm.sh ${W}/p4000.java hadur117.mini.JayLexi 0.4p4000

confirm | sh ./bench-top20.sh ${C} --set kitlab/mini-mid-field.txt --seeds 10 --seed-base 9700 --arms plans/jaylexi-mid.arms --out ${W}/run --label jaylexi-mid --shuffle-jobs
  after: prep
  watch:
  stop: fails 30
  stop: dead 8
  stop: skips 60 over 200
  stop: stall 30m
  stop: aa after 20%
  stop: futility p1,p4 below 0 after 20%

gate | python3 ../data/tools/multiarm.py ${W}/run/arms.tsv --out ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_jaylexi-mid.md && printf '\n## Whole field\n\nThe panel stands for 330 of 669 pairings: the whole-field APS gain of each arm is its vs-ref difference and interval x 0.49.\n' >> ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_jaylexi-mid.md && { [ ! -f ${W}/run/EARLY-STOP.md ] || cat ${W}/run/EARLY-STOP.md >> ${OUT}/$(date +%Y-%m-%d)_jaylexi-mid.md; }
  after: confirm

pr | bash tools/open_results_pr.sh claude/pc-jaylexi-mid-results "JayLexi mid-field surf-row strength (pc-jaylexi-mid)" ${OUT}/*_jaylexi-mid.md
  after: gate
